Third-party data notice:

This software incorporates the AGS4 Data Dictionary — the machine-readable
schema of the AGS4 transfer format (group codes, heading names, data types,
units, status and descriptions) — for all five published editions:

    Standard_dictionary_v4_0_3.ags     AGS4 edition 4.0.3
    Standard_dictionary_v4_0_4.ags     AGS4 edition 4.0.4
    Standard_dictionary_v4_1.ags       AGS4 edition 4.1
    Standard_dictionary_v4_1_1.ags     AGS4 edition 4.1.1
    Standard_dictionary_v4_2.ags       AGS4 edition 4.2

That data is © The Association of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental
Specialists (AGS), all rights reserved. It is reference data for the
published AGS4 transfer-format standard, redistributed here as a documented
decision by the repository owner — see
`rust-packages/laterite-ags4-validator/data/PROVENANCE.md` for the source,
the retrieval provenance and the reasoning.

HOW THE DATA IS DISTRIBUTED — this differs by artefact, and the difference
matters if you are looking for it:

  * In a SOURCE distribution the five files above are present, verbatim, at
    `rust-packages/laterite-ags4-validator/data/`.

  * In a COMPILED distribution — the `laterite` Python wheel, the
    `@laterite/native-*` npm packages, the wasm bundle, the `lat` CLI, the
    `laterite_ags4` DuckDB extension — they are NOT present as files. The
    five editions are projected into a single `ags_dictionary.json` and
    embedded into the binary at compile time (as an `include_str!` constant
    and as generated lookup tables). The AGS content, including every
    heading description verbatim, is therefore inside the compiled artefact
    even though no dictionary file appears alongside it.

This MIT licence covers the source code of this repository. It does not
purport to relicense the AGS dictionary data.
